WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.460
There's a phrase that Carl Gustav Jung often emphasized.

2
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.900
Chance is only the way God's design hides itself.

3
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:19.220
And behind these thoughts there's neither superstition nor an attempt to find some artificial meaning in everything — quite the opposite.

4
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:29.740
Jung deeply believed that nothing we experience, neither meetings nor losses, neither moments of joy nor sorrow, is without meaning.

5
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:42.160
Everything that happens to us happens not without reason, and what we call coincidences is actually part of a delicate and complex web of meanings that life weaves through us.

6
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.800
Jung called this phenomenon synchronicity.

7
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:56.660
It is the moment when two seemingly unrelated phenomena meet in our experience and leave a deep symbolic impression.

8
00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:03.520
There is no external causal connection, but there is an inner meaning that won't let us go.

9
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:13.380
Say you think about an old friend you haven't seen for years, and the next day you meet him completely by chance in another city.

10
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:23.920
Or you stumble on a book that answers exactly a question that had tormented you for days. And no, these are not simple coincidences, these are messages.

11
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:38.580
For Jung such a situation can bring us closer to ourselves, make us stop and ask: what has been set in motion within me, what truth am I ready to hear.

12
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:51.940
Jung viewed a person not as an isolated loner in a chaotic world, but as a spiritual being connected to something greater: to the unconscious, to the Self, to collective experience.

13
00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:58.820
And therefore nothing in our life comes without a calling, without a lesson, without a purpose.

14
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:06.540
When we find ourselves in painful situations, it's easy to think life has forgotten us, that everything is meaningless.

15
00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:14.400
But precisely then, setting aside the idea of chance, we can begin to see a deeper story.

16
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.740
Perhaps we needed to lose something in order to learn to rely on ourselves.

17
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:32.880
Perhaps someone left us because they could no longer walk our path. Perhaps a door closed not so that we would suffer, but so that we would finally go where our place always was.

18
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:38.860
Jung believed that our inner world is constantly in dialogue with the outer.

19
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:45.200
Our thoughts, feelings, aspirations — all this shapes what happens to us.

20
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:56.240
This is not mechanics in the spirit of "think positive and all will be well," but a deeper understanding that the world around us reflects our inner dynamics.

21
00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:05.960
If we live in fear, we will attract situations that amplify it, not so that we suffer, but so that we recognize it and overcome it.

22
00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.480
Synchronicities are calls from the unconscious.

23
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.220
They don't come every day, but when they appear, they leave a mark.

24
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:22.500
These are the moments that remind us that we are being guided, that we're on the right path, that order exists even when chaos seems to reign.

25
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:34.280
These moments are not proof that life is easy, but that it has meaning. They are not a guarantee that pain will spare us, but a confirmation that this pain is not in vain.

26
00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:42.160
Nothing happens by chance, because we are part of a deeper order, a structure that surpasses our everyday understanding.

27
00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:49.140
Every experience, every person who has touched us is here to wake us, to move us and to guide us.

28
00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:53.550
Jung did not believe in mere survival, but in development.

29
00:03:53.550 --> 00:04:00.420
Life, according to him, is a great journey to the Self, to the authentic, whole self.

30
00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:08.180
And this journey cannot be chaotic: every step, even the hardest, is part of our growth.

31
00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:18.330
When we begin to look at life through such eyes, we change perspective: we no longer ask "why is this happening to me," but ask "what is this teaching me."

32
00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:22.870
We don't run from failures, but see in them a part of the plan.

33
00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:28.980
We don't blame others for our suffering, but look for inner causes and lessons.

34
00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.430
And then, even in the quietest moments, we feel that we are being guided.

35
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:52.460
Jung urges us to believe in symbolism, to be open to signs, to listen to our dreams, because the unconscious never stops speaking, and when something we don't understand happens, it doesn't mean it's meaningless, only that we aren't yet ready to grasp it.

36
00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:59.160
In silence, in intuition, in unexpected meetings, life is always teaching us something.

37
00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.380
Nothing happens by chance.

38
00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:09.440
The people we've met are part of this path: some to hold us, others to wound us, still others to wake us.

39
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.140
The situations we've been through are part of this map.

40
00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:19.180
Pain taught us compassion, loneliness taught us the value of connection.

41
00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.720
Loss taught us to appreciate presence.

42
00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:29.840
And when you look back, you'll see: what you thought was an end was only a new beginning.

43
00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:35.220
Where you were broken, a part of your strength quietly grew.

44
00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:43.380
What you called failure was a signpost that led you away from the wrong path to show you the right one.

45
00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:50.200
And what you saw as chance was the answer to a question you didn't even know you had asked.

46
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:58.620
How many times did it seem to you that nothing was happening to you, while in fact everything was falling into place exactly as needed?

47
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:09.900
How many times did you meet someone at the right moment, read a phrase that opened a new understanding for you, or experienced a failure that later saved your soul?

48
00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:16.640
Jung reminds us: everything that irritates us in others can lead us to understand ourselves.

49
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:24.870
In the same way, everything that happens to us, especially what we call chance, leads us closer to our true self.

50
00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:33.880
Not because we must believe in miracles, but because we ourselves are part of a deeper order in which chance does not exist.

51
00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:51.420
So don't dismiss these quiet moments when something coincides, don't ignore intuition, don't turn away from little signs that seem unimportant, because perhaps precisely then life is calling you to slow down, to listen, to set out on a new path.

52
00:06:51.420 --> 00:07:01.260
In synchronicities, as Jung called them, a message is hidden, and it doesn't always come when you're looking for it, but when you're ready to understand it.

53
00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:07.680
Believe that everything has its own order, that nothing comes too early or late.

54
00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:15.360
Life may not unfold the way you imagined, but it always unfolds exactly as you need.

55
00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:30.960
At times you'll think you've lost your way, lost your compass, that everything happening is meaningless, and then, over time, you'll understand that precisely then you were closest to what your soul was seeking.

56
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:36.350
There's no need to rush things, to cling frantically to plans.

57
00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:47.820
Let go, breathe, rely on the inner rhythm that quietly whispers to you when it's time to go, when to stop, when to let go, and when to embrace.

58
00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:57.880
For life is not a linear trajectory, but circles, spirals, a return to yourself through people, lessons and unusual paths.

59
00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:00.940
And every such return is precious.

60
00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.280
Your life is exactly where it needs to be.

61
00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:14.760
Perhaps you don't see all the answers now, perhaps circumstances confuse you, but meaning is found not in chaotic searching, but in trust.

62
00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:23.860
In allowing life to unfold and in believing that every moment has its place in the mosaic of your wholeness.

63
00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:38.940
And so, when you stop and look back, you won't see coincidences, you'll see the invisible threads that guided you, you'll see traces that you didn't understand then, but which led you exactly here.

64
00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:45.410
And as Jung once said, everything that happens to you happens to you.

65
00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.760
You are a part of it.

66
00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:55.380
You are an important part of a larger whole, and so believe, because nothing, absolutely nothing happens by chance.

67
00:08:55.380 --> 00:09:02.460
My dears, tell us, have you ever experienced a coincidence that changed your life?

68
00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:08.940
Do you believe that certain people enter your life not without reason, at exactly the right moment?

69
00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:15.780
And wasn't what you wanted but didn't get actually your greatest gift?

70
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.400
Share your thoughts with us in the comments.

71
00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:22.260
I wish you peace and all the best!